# Line-ending normalisation (added 2026-10-04; see docs/dev/checks-and-ci.md, "Line endings").
#
# Every text file is stored with LF in the repository and checked out with LF, whatever the machine's
# core.autocrlf says. The index was already 100% LF when this was added, so it changes no committed content; it
# stops CRLF from ever entering the repo (CI on Linux, a clone with autocrlf=false, a tool writing CRLF) and stops
# the CRLF/LF diff churn. Existing working-tree files keep their current endings until git rewrites them
# (checkout / reset); staging a CRLF or mixed file converts it to LF in the index, which is not a content change.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows scripts keep CRLF.
*.bat   text eol=crlf
*.cmd   text eol=crlf
*.ps1   text eol=crlf

# Binary: never convert, never diff as text.
*.wasm  binary
*.png   binary
*.png~  binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.webp  binary
*.ico   binary
*.cur   binary
*.glb   binary
*.bin   binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.zip   binary
*.gz    binary
*.frogmarks binary
*.frogcart  binary
